# Workflow and testing (from AUTONOMOUS_BRIEF.md §5, README.md, PROGRESS.md and BLOCKERS.md)

## Gates (before every commit)
- `flutter analyze` must be **clean** (no issues).
- `flutter test` must **pass** (currently 50 tests: crypto, auth, calculator, storage,
  second-phone, branding, app-flow / second-phone widget tests).
- Add or extend tests for any change to crypto, auth, storage, the calculator, the second phone
  or branding.

## Build (this box)
```bash
export PATH=/workspace/tools/flutter/bin:$PATH   # Flutter 3.47 stable
flutter pub get
flutter analyze
flutter test
flutter build apk --release                                    # universal (~55 MB, debug-signed)
flutter build apk --release --target-platform android-arm64    # arm64-only APK (v0.2 test build)
aapt2 dump permissions build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk   # must list only USE_BIOMETRIC (+ AndroidX internal)
```
- The Android SDK is in `/workspace/tools/android-sdk`, and JDK 17 is in `/workspace/tools/jdk17`.
- The `android/` project is committed. `bootstrap.sh` only re-creates it if missing.
- The repo docs only say "arm64 release APK built". The `--target-platform android-arm64` flag
  above is the standard Flutter way to build it.

## Commits and PRs
- Code every day. Work does not stop when the owner is away.
  (TR: "Her gün kod yazılır. Proje sahibi yokken de iş durmaz.")
- Make a small, descriptive commit at every meaningful step: `feat:`, `fix:`, `test:`, `docs:`
  (scopes are OK, e.g. `feat(android):`).
- Open **one PR at the end of each week**. Every PR must include:
  - a one-line summary per changed file
  - the test/analyze result
  - the list of remaining work
- Feature branches PR into the previous line (`v0.2-calculator-workprofile` → `mvp-v1` → `main`).
- Never force-push or rewrite history (BLOCKER).

## Docs to keep updated
- `DECISIONS.md`: add a dated row (date, decision, why) for every non-trivial decision. No
  approval needed for normal decisions.
- `PROGRESS.md`: **one paragraph per day**.
- `BLOCKERS.md`: every risky or irreversible step you stopped at, and every owner decision needed.
- Keep `README.md`, `PRIVACY.md` and `docs/PLAY_COMPLIANCE.md` in sync when features or
  permissions change.

## Localization
- Every user-facing string goes in **both** `lib/l10n/tr.dart` and `lib/l10n/en.dart`
  (map-based, `L10nScope`).
- Android resource strings: `values` (EN default) + `values-tr`.

## Device test matrix (open, see BLOCKERS.md)
There is no device on this box. The Second phone flow (provisioning, the signed cross-profile
trampoline, freeze/unfreeze, clone fallback, removal) is untested on real hardware. Test on:
- **Xiaomi** (MIUI/HyperOS, often blocks work profiles → check the Second space / Private space fallback)
- **Samsung** (Secure Folder coexists)
- **Pixel** (reference AOSP behaviour; a Pixel emulator also works for review)
